      children: "This pattern leverages the fact that most code generation tasks in production aren't creative exercises-they're implementations of known interfaces within established architectural patterns. By specifying interfaces, types, tests, and constraints upfront, we eliminate the exploratory phase where agents might generate multiple implementation approaches, compare them, and iterate. The agent generates a plan conformant to the contract, implements it, and validates once. This typically reduces token consumption by 50-70% compared to unconstrained \"implement feature X\" prompts."
